Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: small music player for GNOME, inspired by Amberol
 Ithaca plays your music, and nothing else. It does not manage a library:
 open songs, folders or playlists and they are added to the play queue,
 which is remembered between sessions.
  - large cover art, waveform progress bar, gapless playback;
  - shuffle, repeat, search in the queue;
  - playlists (.m3u, .m3u8, .xspf, .pls) and web radios;
  - ReplayGain, media keys and GNOME panel controls (MPRIS);
  - background playback with a tray icon.
 It follows the desktop theme (Adwaita, light/dark, accent colour), or
 optionally tints the window after the album cover.
